WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.175
Let’s walk through Follow move, phase, and timer

00:00:03.175 --> 00:00:03.337
.

00:00:03.337 --> 00:00:07.312
Anchor every facilitation decision to the shared exercise window.

00:00:07.312 --> 00:00:09.438
Name the active state for the room, then keep

00:00:09.438 --> 00:00:11.387
the deck and handoff aligned with it;

00:00:11.387 --> 00:00:14.262
timing context should never be inferred later.

00:00:14.262 --> 00:00:17.375
On this slide, the header shows Strategic Orientation before

00:00:17.375 --> 00:00:20.163
Move 1, then the active move, phase,

00:00:20.163 --> 00:00:23.425
countdown timer, and running or paused state.

00:00:23.425 --> 00:00:27.050
Use it to timestamp notes against the current exercise window

00:00:27.050 --> 00:00:27.212
.

00:00:27.735 --> 00:00:30.935
In practice, confirm the current window before recording a

00:00:30.935 --> 00:00:35.610
turning point so later review can reconstruct cause and sequence

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:35.785
.

00:00:35.785 --> 00:00:39.297
Use the highlighted Live tracker area as your visual reference

00:00:39.297 --> 00:00:41.010
while you complete this check.
